meanwhile the big story yesterday the  cdc updating its indoor mass guidance  now recommending vaccinated americans  put the mass back on too  especially in areas with high  transmission and even advising  universal masking everybody in a school  needs to wear a mask even if they've had  the shot  here with reaction we've got fox news  medical contributor dr mark siegel we've  got a high school teacher out in  california  and author of the upcoming book hollowed  out jeremy adams  and new jersey mom of three nila hadley  good morning to all of you  good morning good morning neil neil  let's start with you because you're on  the front lines you got three  three kids going back to school in about  a month month and a half  when they heard they they're gonna have  to wear a mask  from sun up to sun down in the in the  school building  what did they say my son's  first reaction is he's not going back to  school  my daughters are not happy at all  it's something we're going to have to  discuss but my kids are  i don't want to say a mess but they're  pretty upset about it  what do you mean your son is not going  to go back to school  so last year he had a  secondary infection he had a reaction to  a mask which turned into a full-blown  skin infection on his face oh my  goodness  um he is left with a couple scars still  and um he  uh he he doesn't want to go through that  again i i don't blame him  all right it was a very painful  experience absolutely  uh jeremy you're out in california  you're in baker bakersfield california  uh they're saying that you know you're  gonna have to do it in california you  know governor  newsom is gonna say that but the whole  reason you  got the shot was so you wouldn't have to  wear the mask around the kids and now  you're gonna have to wear the mask  around the kids  jeremy it's absolutely frustrating i'll  be honest with you  uh the truth of the matter is you know  i'm not a doctor i'm not a scientist i  can't tell you if we're  we need to be doing this from a  scientific perspective but i can tell  you  that teaching in a mask is awful it's  ridiculously hard especially  if you're trying to you know use the  humanity of the classroom use humor use  your  facial expressions reach the kids and  these kids need to get back to a normal  situation  the last 16 months has not been good for  them and they they weren't doing  particularly great before you know which  is why i wrote the book hollowed out  so all the teachers i talked to  yesterday who got the vaccines because  we  know these kids needed to get back to  normal it's demoralized  absolutely and dr siegel you know  parents  are struggling to try to explain to  their kids okay this is what we're going  to have to do but you look at neil's  story she's got the son  who wound up with the the face infection  which is something a lot of people don't  think about because you're wearing it  all day  uh and and it takes its toll on your  face  and on your psyche that's right steve  there's big downsides to mass that have  to be factored in  and there's the idea of what kind of  mask are you wearing because if you're  wearing an n95 with a formal seal  that works really well but kids are not  going to tolerate that  and and so the idea is it should never  be a mandate it might be something i  you recommend if there's a lot of virus  but there isn't a lot of spread  in schools there isn't a lot of spread  among young children and you know star  reporter peter ducey  when she when he talked to jen zaki  yesterday  you got this feeling of a condescending  tone didn't you  we know and you don't we know and we're  going to tell you what to do so the  mistake the administration is making  is mixing masking with vaccines as you  know as  as the high school teacher just said i  mean you know  vaccines work masks shouldn't be  mentioned in the same sentence  yeah dr siegel so many people are  hesitant to take the vaccine  but joe biden said you get the vaccine  you can take down the mask  and now of course uh that turns out it's  not going to be the  suggestion going forward everybody's  gonna have to wear a mask regardless of  vaccination status  but also you know the fda has not given  final approval and there  are probably millions of americans who  said well i'm if the fda the federal  government  is not saying it's a hundred percent  safe with final approval i'm not going  to get it  so why is the government taking so long  this is an  all hands on deck situation  this is unprecedented and even though it  usually takes the fda  a long time in this case my opinion and  i think yours is they should get  off their duff and do it right now and  get it approved to send that vote of  confidence  because over 300 million doses have  already been given out it's not like  they don't have the data steve  they got the data they've got to move  fast and they got to license the vaccine  and then you're going to see a lot more  people taking it that are on the fence  yeah neela you know i remember when our  our kids were living in the house and  they were getting ready for school  right about now they'd start getting  excited about school you know  let's go get some new clothes and let's  go to staples and we'll get all the  spiral notebooks and stuff like this but  given the fact that now it sounds like  we're going to have to have the kids  wearing the masks again  that just made your job tougher getting  the kids out the door  absolutely it has i  i'm hoping he's going to be exempt  because of the severity of his  skin and how bad his face was  i mean like i said there's still some  scarring so  i am hoping that the doctors uh  recognize this and they agree with me  uh and then hopefully he'll be able to  go back to school  yeah like a normal kid uh as far as my  girls go  my older one's going into eighth grade  she said mom i don't want to be  homeschooled for eighth grade  yeah i don't blame her and then my sixth  grader this is this is  uh the social aspect of school is just  as important as the  education absolutely and jeremy you're  out in california  how much of an impact do you think the  teachers unions  had in convincing the government to say  everybody's got to wear a mask  well yeah i can't speak to the cta but i  can tell you most of the teachers that i  know  got vaccinated for a variety of reasons  but the number one reason is  as our parent just said a second ago  we've got to get back to a sense of  normalcy uh you know steve i'm  i'm a bit of a of a classroom romantic i  think that the the most certain door to  the american dream no matter what your  background is  is a high quality education which means  we need our teachers to be at their  absolute best  now the last year of learning for our  students has not been pretty you know  they've been behind  anonymous zoom calls sure sitting in bed  you know oftentimes texting as they uh  take classes  and we need to get back to a sense of  normalcy for sure we sure do and dr  siegel exit question this is only a  recommendation it's going to be up to  state and local leaders whether or not  your locality  actually says mask up everybody right  right and theoretically it's only  supposed to be in areas of a lot of  spread but kids spread more covet  outside school than in school and i  already told you they don't spread it  much in school  the danger is that it's going to be  extended to areas where there's not even  any virus around  yeah you're right there's a lot going on  uh dr  siegel teachers have to get vaccinated  absolutely  everybody who can get vaccinated should  dr siegel jeremy  neela thank you all for sharing your  stories today  thank you very much i'm steve ducey i'm  brian kilny and i'm ainsley earhart and  click here to subscribe to the fox news  youtube page to catch our hottest  interviews  and most compelling analysis

